From: libpldm portable build maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] tests: Append downstream device record byte by byte

Developed against upstream be4f63e36408921e76d868593176377de84e945e,
after patches 1-6 in this series.

Ubuntu GCC 14 diagnoses the vector range insertion in makePkgV1_1_0()
as a stringop-overflow at -O3, blocking the warnings-as-errors build.
Append the same record bytes individually to avoid that optimized
range-insertion path. Keep all package-parser tests and warning checks
enabled; neither the fixture contents nor production code change.

diff --git a/tests/unit/bindings/cpp/firmware-update-test-v1-1-0.cpp b/tests/unit/bindings/cpp/firmware-update-test-v1-1-0.cpp
--- a/tests/unit/bindings/cpp/firmware-update-test-v1-1-0.cpp
+++ b/tests/unit/bindings/cpp/firmware-update-test-v1-1-0.cpp
@@ -100,7 +100,10 @@
 
     // DownstreamDeviceIDRecordCount
     pkg.push_back(0x01);
-    pkg.insert(pkg.end(), ddevidarea.begin(), ddevidarea.end());
+    for (const auto byte : ddevidarea)
+    {
+        pkg.push_back(byte);
+    }
 
     const auto clos = appendComponentImageInfoArea1(pkg);
 
